    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`, `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:142-244`), listing each validation (V) and side-effect (S) in the exact order they execute.\n\n## Before the method body\n\n1. **(V) Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 117/142): caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected before any logic runs.\n2. **(V) Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 the generated `OwnersApi` contract validates the incoming `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid`) before the method is entered; any constraint violations on the DTO fields are rejected here.\n\n## Inside the method body (in order)\n\n3. **(S) Map DTO \u2192 entity** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` builds the `Owner` (line 146).\n4. **(S) Default the registration date** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is null, set it to `LocalDate.now()` (lines 147-149).\n5. **(V) Registration date not in the future** \u2014 if the (supplied) registration date is after today \u2192 **400 Bad Request** (lines 151-153).\n6. **(S) Roll registration date to a business day** \u2014 `toBusinessDay(...)`: Saturday \u2192 +2, Sunday \u2192 +1, weekday unchanged (line 154).\n7. **(V) Per-day volume cap** \u2014 count existing owners already registered on that (rolled) date; if `>= 100` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests** (lines 155-162).\n8. **(S) Normalize address** \u2014 `addressNormalizer.normalize(...)` (line 163).\n9. **(V) Address not blank** \u2014 if the normalized address is blank \u2192 **400** (lines 164-166).\n10. **(S) Store normalized address** \u2014 `owner.setAddress(address)` (line 167).\n11. **(S) Normalize telephone** \u2014 `telephoneNormalizer.normalize(...)` (line 168).\n12. **(V) Telephone present/parseable** \u2014 if normalized telephone is null \u2192 **400** (lines 169-171).\n13. **(V) Telephone national-number length** \u2014 if `!hasValidNationalNumberLength(...)` \u2192 **400** (lines 172-174).\n14. **(S) Store normalized telephone** \u2014 `owner.setTelephone(telephone)` (line 175).\n15. **Email handling (only if email is non-null)** (lines 176-187):\n    - **(S)** trim the email;\n    - **(V)** if it doesn't match `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 **400**;\n    - **(V)** if its domain is in `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail, case-insensitive) \u2192 **400**;\n    - **(S)** store the email lower-cased.\n16. **Postcode handling (only if postcode is non-null)** (lines 191-197):\n    - **(V)** if it isn't exactly 4 digits (`POSTCODE_PATTERN`) **or** isn't valid for the owner's city (`cityRegionResolver.isPostcodeValidForCity`) \u2192 **400**.\n17. **(S) Assign household id** \u2014 `owner.setHouseholdId(householdResolver.householdId(owner))`, deterministic from normalized last name + postcode (line 203).\n18. **(V) Household-duplicate rule** \u2014 if the household already exists **and** the `sharesHousehold` flag is not true \u2192 **409 Conflict** (lines 204-212).\n19. **(V) Hard duplicate (identity key)** \u2014 `isDuplicateOwner(owner)`: if any existing owner has the same `identityKey` (normalized telephone | email | householdId) \u2192 **409** (lines 213-215).\n20. **(V) Per-city cap** \u2014 count existing owners in the same normalized city; if `>= 50` \u2192 **409** (lines 216-222).\n21. **(S) Set customer code** \u2014 `customerCode(owner)` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city + SHA-256 prefix of telephone+lastName) (line 223).\n22. **(S) Set namesake count** \u2014 number of existing owners sharing first+last name, case-insensitive (line 224).\n23. **(S) Set membership number** \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from the registration year (line 225).\n24. **(S) Set bulk-signup warning** \u2014 `true` if more than 80 owners already registered that day (line 226).\n25. **(S) Compute & set soft-duplicate flags** \u2014 unless it's a declared household member, `possibleDuplicateOf(owner)` finds an existing owner with the same normalized last name + same postcode but a different telephone (lowest id); then `setPossibleDuplicate(...)` and `setPossibleDuplicateOf(...)` (lines 233-235).\n26. **(S) Persist the owner** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 236).\n27. **(S) Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` emits an audit line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membership level (lines 237-239).\n28. **(S) Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created** (lines 240-243).\n\n### Notes on ordering\n- The validations short-circuit in this exact sequence, so the **first** failing check determines the response status \u2014 e.g. a future registration date (400) is reported before the per-day cap (429), which is reported before any address/telephone/email/postcode checks.\n- Several side-effects mutate the entity **before** later validations run (address, telephone, email, householdId are all normalized/set before the duplicate and city-cap checks), and the rate-limit counts at steps 7 and 24 are both derived from `ownersCreatedThatDay` captured at step 7."
